{:edb/db-before-t 632 :edb/db-after-t 633 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533945 50 #inst "2026-10-05T15:54:35.253Z" 13194139533945 true] [17592186087595 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267693 13194139533945 true] [17592186087595 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267700 13194139533945 true] [17592186087595 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267707 13194139533945 true] [17592186087595 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267749 13194139533945 true] [17592186087595 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267770 13194139533945 true] [17592186087596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267728 13194139533945 true] [17592186087596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267735 13194139533945 true] [17592186087596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267742 13194139533945 true] [17592186087596 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267763 13194139533945 true] [17592186087597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267714 13194139533945 true] [17592186087597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267721 13194139533945 true] [17592186087597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267756 13194139533945 true] [17592186087597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267777 13194139533945 true] [17592186087597 1020 #edb/ref 17592186267784 13194139533945 true] [17592186088385 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186088385 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =3 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(0-2)^{2} & =3 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+4 & =3 \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x+3)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x+3)^{2}=-1.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/cb8a943a6f6cfd49e47c193f5379e06fd166cd17087c890233b42a7e1e7d2b89.png)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267693 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267694 13194139533945 true] [17592186267693 1089 "q-15471" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267693 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186267693 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/27e00721ccddb4982dac95216cdd990af311e27e5300154b7133b36fca42f3e1.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8,$ shown above." 13194139533945 true] [17592186267693 1113 #uuid "acf4151c-fa50-5ea8-9858-28080dd21e43" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267693 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(0-1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+1 & =8 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =7 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{7} \\\\ x & =3\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(3-\\sqrt{7},0)$ and $(3+\\sqrt{7},0).$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267695 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267696 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267697 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267698 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267699 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267699 13194139533945 true] [17592186267694 1110 #uuid "45b74600-dd65-5daf-a0bb-21f135aef473" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267695 1034 "$(1,0)$ and $(10,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267695 1111 #uuid "fcdf2158-3d8a-5577-a89c-c0df108c953b" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267696 1034 "$(2,0)$ and $(12,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267696 1111 #uuid "dcc06385-baa7-55c8-8c76-d5a77b5f8a20" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267697 1034 "$(3-\\sqrt{6},0)$ and $(3+\\sqrt{6},0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267697 1111 #uuid "d028f383-5074-5ba8-a4ea-3fa28fe1ad90" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267698 1034 "$(3-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(3+\\sqrt{5},0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267698 1111 #uuid "c68c7ff9-ef71-5444-8b2e-bd8e379d5ea2" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267699 1034 "$(3-\\sqrt{7},0)$ and $(3+\\sqrt{7},0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267699 1111 #uuid "546f2032-21f5-59b2-a85b-59b5f7a0dce3" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267700 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267701 13194139533945 true] [17592186267700 1089 "q-15681" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267700 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186267700 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/13b9598c77cd522d0d3aeee4f5abd2390822431aa49ed787b73a110113ab821c.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=25,$ shown above." 13194139533945 true] [17592186267700 1113 #uuid "128b9cef-763e-5aac-a6f0-9eae06355cd4" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267700 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+{0}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =25 \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{25} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-9,0)$ and $(1,0).$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267702 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267703 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267704 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267705 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267706 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267704 13194139533945 true] [17592186267701 1110 #uuid "12d6d6df-5bb6-5bc5-8e62-6a1b35ee1cf5" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267702 1034 "$(-9,0)$ and $(1.5,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267702 1111 #uuid "6c110050-6686-51ea-b186-39ebaa097fc0" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267703 1034 "$(-8,0)$ and $(1,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267703 1111 #uuid "53a5b66d-7124-5fb4-89e2-22105b1af00b" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267704 1034 "$(-9,0)$ and $(1,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267704 1111 #uuid "0b27c99d-2398-5a19-97c5-cd11f2ed14fe" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267705 1034 "$(-10,0)$ and $(1,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267705 1111 #uuid "a563ed93-7ce7-57eb-a026-d74c058e5bb6" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267706 1034 "$(-9,0)$ and $(0.8,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267706 1111 #uuid "a70833ad-924a-544c-94e9-73e797db0e89" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267707 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267708 13194139533945 true] [17592186267707 1089 "q-15684" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267707 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186267707 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/c6d356b443128da569a6b60065769cdb56e2e0059db7b146a3c4035d18a32228.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=45,$ shown above." 13194139533945 true] [17592186267707 1113 #uuid "1d50f11f-d6f2-5605-88f1-8c45f7404cb9" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267707 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =45 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(0-3)^{2} & =45 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+9 & =45 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{36} \\\\ x & =1\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(7,0).$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267709 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267710 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267711 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267712 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267713 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267712 13194139533945 true] [17592186267708 1110 #uuid "d38519d4-cc52-5902-9cf3-70f4e5db357c" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267709 1034 "$(-5,0)$ and $(8,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267709 1111 #uuid "bb9dad29-b3f6-5ffd-b193-ffc7c83f5a12" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267710 1034 "$(-5.5,0)$ and $(7.5,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267710 1111 #uuid "d6982368-5a66-5f9d-9a66-f5fdb0984bea" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267711 1034 "$(-6,0)$ and $(8,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267711 1111 #uuid "27bad4bf-ea6b-5517-8b75-4bf1337a756d" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267712 1034 "$(-5,0)$ and $(7,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267712 1111 #uuid "d7258ddb-0a7e-558c-9131-5108b75c2a7a" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267713 1034 "$(-6,0)$ and $(7,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267713 1111 #uuid "5e105f04-51ef-5fab-90ac-f2f2958c85cf" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267714 1017 #edb/ref 175