ue] [17592186267722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267726 13194139533945 true] [17592186267722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267727 13194139533945 true] [17592186267722 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267722 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267722 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267727 13194139533945 true] [17592186267722 1110 #uuid "12d7b9fc-d7a3-5bd7-a0a9-50ebbbfef39b" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267723 1034 "$(0,4-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,4+\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267723 1111 #uuid "365c2cc9-c09c-5186-a5b2-cbc1b37e4c50" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267724 1034 "$(0,6-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,6+\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267724 1111 #uuid "b7767f20-469a-5b49-9722-5ca0d4953b10" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267725 1034 "$(0,5-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,5+\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267725 1111 #uuid "2d992dcf-09b9-53f5-8bca-d6c180748bcb" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267726 1034 "$(0,5-\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,5+\\sqrt{5})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267726 1111 #uuid "4058f0e9-0f05-56bc-9830-4c394c1368e3" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267727 1034 "$(0,4-\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,4+\\sqrt{5})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267727 1111 #uuid "fa03cb03-a289-5f78-ab13-b8ebd0c4b8c5" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267728 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267729 13194139533945 true] [17592186267728 1089 "q-160272" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267728 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186267728 1100 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the circle $(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=9.$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267728 1113 #uuid "26d19767-6cb6-5671-822b-38e5862a3bbc" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267728 1145 "When the circle intercepts the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$\n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $y$, if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (0-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ 16+(y+4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(y+4)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $y,$ there is no $y$ such that $(y+4)^{2}=-7.$ Therefore, the circle does not intercept the $y$-axis at any point, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/2442ca38770f2f82e2e9c536632e8474adb75e04504a4273987989bb3d81b282.png)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267730 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267731 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267732 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267733 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267734 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267732 13194139533945 true] [17592186267729 1110 #uuid "ca2a37aa-af08-58f9-aa50-893dda7203bb" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267730 1034 "(0,2)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267730 1111 #uuid "af74ac86-06fd-5d63-a4e4-45c8bfb8357d" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267731 1034 "$(0,-1)$ and $(0,1)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267731 1111 #uuid "1349e6f0-2289-55e4-93ec-b2ad8f16b6f0" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267732 1034 "The circle has no $y$-intercepts" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267732 1111 #uuid "7a540a32-1f0e-5244-9c2f-533e28055674" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267733 1034 "(0,-4)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267733 1111 #uuid "4a515f53-0ed3-5dca-8ffe-a6fda60873fe" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267734 1034 "$(0,-7)$ and $(0,-1)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267734 1111 #uuid "61a3cfe9-fbfb-501a-9c5c-6eac1308683f" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267735 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267736 13194139533945 true] [17592186267735 1089 "q-160275" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267735 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186267735 1100 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the circle $(x+1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267735 1113 #uuid "8baf38e5-4cac-5611-8d4f-60ea7baafdea" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267735 1145 "When the circle intercepts the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$\n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $y$, if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ (0+1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1+(y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(y+2)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $y,$ there is no $y$ such that $(y+2)^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, the circle does not intercept the $y$-axis at any point, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/86f198b30096cf3106186ee2595b61c21be000e8e6223c5b42ee453ba1b9fe4a.png)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267737 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267738 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267739 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267740 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267741 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267740 13194139533945 true] [17592186267736 1110 #uuid "7067af39-0c6e-514e-aa79-74762099ea15" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267737 1034 "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267737 1111 #uuid "f80d2f64-e788-5621-b7da-23c2453a1f04" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267738 1034 "$(0,-\\frac{1}{4})$ and $(0,\\frac{3}{4})$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267738 1111 #uuid "1e0ec51b-3660-51a8-8a40-4363ad19d3e0" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267739 1034 "(0,-\\frac{3}{4})" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267739 1111 #uuid "0cac8261-80b4-5649-bf1c-1e69a56d7d3c" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267740 1034 "The circle has no $y$-intercepts" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267740 1111 #uuid "68c8d89a-acbc-5908-ac1e-e86036864292" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267741 1034 "(0,-2)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267741 1111 #uuid "fef2a79c-2a6d-5510-964f-0c0548484a19" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267742 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267743 13194139533945 true] [17592186267742 1089 "q-160286" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267742 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533945 true] [17592186267742 1100 "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+8x-6y+21=0$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267742 1113 #uuid "75748ec5-c482-5439-91c2-00c020d6415b" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267742 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+8x-6y+21 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2}+8x-6\\cdot 0+21 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x+21 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x+16+21 & =0+16 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+21 & =16 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x+4)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x+4)^{2}=-5.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/53b8e33665ee3ba0b36d04c9d82715b18505c501db535ecf4a40c48c81814584.png)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267744 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267745 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267746 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267747 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267748 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267746 13194139533945 true] [17592186267743 1110 #uuid "8a2d023b-07b4-58b0-a1cf-3b4676decdb6" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267744 1034 "$(-5,0)$ and $(12,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267744 1111 #uuid "617357b4-289b-538c-b217-0c0ded8e0779" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267745 1034 "(4,0)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267745 1111 #uuid "8d97a31f-4600-5899-8782-618d32a0bde2" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267746 1034 "The circle has no $x$-intercepts" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267746 1111 #uuid "c2f25041-4a4a-51d2-990a-8422d912e219" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267747 1034 "$(-6,0)$ and $(-2,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267747 1111 #uuid "431c93d4-6b45-5cc5-9206-0dd6e6594267" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267748 1034 "(-4,0)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267748 1111 #uuid "296a331e-81c0-521f-b671-4e6e84d7ccc5" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267749 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267750 13194139533945 true] [17592186267749 1089 "q-54228" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533945 true] [17592186267749 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/3f597a8596601b6e53e93e76ba3082d87159ff03b52c2a5a2b3eba5cbf3332ec.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8x+6y+15=0,$ shown above." 13194139533945 true] [17592186267749 1113 #uuid "1aef1d02-462f-5423-aa4a-1388b5adbed6" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267749 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8x+6y+15 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-8x+6\\cdot 0+15 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+15 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+16+15 & =0+16 \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+15 & =16 \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =1 \\\\ x-4 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =4\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(3,0)$ and $(5,0).$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267751 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267752 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267753 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267754 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267755 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267752 13194139533945 true] [17592186267750 1110 #uuid "165a59ce-50e6-5a0d-bad8-003375710839" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267751 1034 "$(3,0)$ and $(4,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267751 1111 #uuid "5a3825ca-450c-5fec-9292-9c6eeb9f2346" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267752 1034 "$(3,0)$ and $(5,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267752 1111 #uuid "7487f0e9-dc1e-550a-a3af-691fe0e777c4" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267753 1034 "$(2,0)$ and $(4,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267753 1111 #uuid "7d1c6651-2b34-51ae-9785-cded765103ae" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267754 1034 "$(2,0)$ and $(5,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267754 1111 #uuid "72d8bfd4-cfc9-5e86-a257-cf5065fcc175" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267755 1034 "$(4,0)$ and $(6,0)$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267755 1111 #uuid "482186d3-3759-5756-9324-f4ce5925a332" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267756 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267757 13194139533945 true] [17592186267756 1089 "q-7541" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267756 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533945 true] [17592186267756 1100 "Find the $y$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=64.$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267756 1113 #uuid "b2b39999-a8e4-57a7-ab96-4715ec5c76ca" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267756 1145 "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ {0}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{64} \\\\ y & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,-8)$ and $(0,8),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/90fc285151a5f549992e3c40ba6cff89532398808d6194fdf7922108b73646ef.png)" 13194139533945 true] [