12=0$" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267763 1113 #uuid "f43a31ca-f582-5ca4-a303-c0af1e9c11d4" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267763 1145 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2x+6y+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-2x+6\\cdot 0+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+1+12 & =0+1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+12 & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x-1)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x-1)^{2}=-11.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/ea1410ea792ac5fb09316bc6d417c2ba46f84c050491b1e351f360eac50deb6c.png)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267765 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267766 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267767 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267768 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267769 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1041 "selection" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267765 13194139533945 true] [17592186267764 1110 #uuid "8d45a237-1e48-5551-a790-007c77780796" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267765 1034 "The circle has no $x$-intercepts" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533945 true] [17592186267765 1111 #uuid "3c77d996-98a0-53e9-8d8e-30d0603083f4" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267766 1034 "(2,0)" 13194139533945 true] [17592186267766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533945 true] [17592186267766 1111 #uuid "ac011ff3-3ebb-5e07-bc82-18c3da00bc3e" 13194139533945 true] [175921